Members Name Description Serial it is a serial line TCP_IP it is a TCP line UDP it is a UDP line ModbusClientLineInfo Protocols.ModbusClientLineInfo &ndash;
Members Name Description DetectionRange Detection Range (s) Retry Retry if device is online PollingDelay Polling Delay (ms) PollingLoopsNumber Polling Loops Number LastPollingLoopTime Last Polling Loop Time (ms) LineType Type of line (Serial or TCP) ModbusProtocolDeviceInfo Protocols.ModbusProtocolDeviceInfo &ndash;
Members Name Description SUPER forceMultipleRegisterWrite Force to use only the multiple writes command for registers. forceMultipleCoilWrite Force to use only the multiple writes command for coils. PeripheralInfo Protocols.PeripheralInfo &ndash;
Members Name Description PeripheralType Peripheral identifier FWRelease FW Version: Major*100 + Minor ProtocolCap Bit 0: Message “r” (Carel protocol only)
Bit 1: crc error control (Carel protocol only)
Bit 2: accepts ‘U’, ‘S’, ‘B’ (Carel protocol only)
Bit 3: The device can switch between Carel and Modbus protocol (Carel and Modbus protocols)
Bit 4: accepts firmware download messages (Carel and Modbus protocols)
Bit 5: accepts EEPROM direct writing messages (Carel and Modbus protocol)
Bit 6: reserved for bootloader
Bit 7: the host of CAN bus board is a client of broadcast CAN bus mode (just for Idronic board)
Bit 8: Exception 5 (ACKNOWLEDGE) managed (Modbus protocol only)
Bit 15: At the end of PeripheralInfo message is added an extension of ProtocolCap HWCode Hardware code (input/output) ExportIfaceCode Code or version of variables&rsquo; database ApplicationRelease Application version ApplicationCode Application code CustomerCode Customer code USMaxVar Analog/Integer Max Var BMaxVAr Digital Max Var ExtendedProtCap This field is present in the PeripheralInfo message
if at least one of these things happens:
1) The bit 15 of ProtocolCap is set to 1;
2) It will be necessary to add other fields in queue, after the field ExtendedProtCap.
It is reserved for future extensions of ProtocolCap field. ProtocolDeviceInfo Protocols.ProtocolDeviceInfo &ndash;
Members Name Description isOnline Sets if the device is online or offline Enabled Enables or disables the device Ident Ident of the device NetworkAddress Current IP or hostname of the device DetectionTimeOut Detection timeout (ms) of the device (see Help for more info) TimeOut Timeout (ms) of the device (see Help for more info) CommandDelay Command delay (ms) of the device (see Help for more info) Zone Zone of the device DeviceError Current device error:
- NoError: Device answered as expected;
- Offline: Device did not answer (offline);
- InvalidPacket: Device answered with an invalid packet;
- ErrorCodeReceived: Device answered with an error code;
- NotYetQueried: Device has yet to be queried. LastErrorInfo Informations about last error received from the device. ErrorsCount Counts the number in which Device Error changes state. CommandsCount Counts the number of times in which the client try to communicate with the server. PollsCount Counts the number of complete poll of server. ReadChangesCount Counts the number of times data is updated from a device. ReportServerID Protocols.ReportServerID &ndash;
