GetMicroSdMode(USINT, System.FileSystem.Enums.MmcModeType) System.FileSystem.Async.GetMicroSdMode &ndash; Get the current operating mode of the SD card. The &lsquo;unit&rsquo; input variable is the number of the peripheral. Its value is &lsquo;0&rsquo; if there is only one micro SD.
The value of the &lsquo;mode&rsquo; variable is set according to the current operating
mode and is taken from &lsquo;MmcModeType&rsquo;.
Returns LIB_FS_OK if the configuration will be applied, LIB_FS_ERR_VOLUME_ACCESS otherwise.
Synopsis DINT GetMicroSdMode(USINT, System.FileSystem.Enums.MmcModeType) [Input] USINT unit;
[InOut] System.FileSystem.Enums.MmcModeType mode;
+----------------------------------------+| System.FileSystem.Async.GetMicroSdMode || |USINT-| unit |System.FileSystem.Enums.MmcModeType-| mode------------------------------mode |-System.FileSystem.Enums.MmcModeType+----------------------------------------+Parameters Name Type Description unit USINT Number of the MMC peripheral mode System.FileSystem.Enums.MmcModeType mode of the MMC peripheral Examples (* This example shows how to: - set and get the mode of the MMC peripheral - enable the MMC peripheral - write a test file on it *) USING System.UI; USING System.FileSystem; USING System.FileSystem.Enums; USING System.Timer; VAR_GLOBAL enable : BOOL := FALSE; ready : DINT(-1..2) := -1; mode : MmcModeType(MmcModeType#MMC_MODE_EXTERNAL_DRIVE..MmcModeType#MMC_MODE_PUBLIC_PARTITION) := MmcModeType#MMC_MODE_EXTERNAL_DRIVE; error : DINT(-20..0) := System.FileSystem.ErrorCode.LIB_FS_OK; write_file : USINT := 0; END_VAR PROGRAM Main VAR first_run : UINT := 1; current_mode : MmcModeType; current_enable : BOOL := FALSE; partition : System.FileSystem.Enums.PartitionType := System.FileSystem.Enums.PartitionType#SdCard; current_file_number : UINT := 0; filepath : STRING[32]; openmode : System.FileSystem.Enums.FS_OpenMode := System.FileSystem.Enums.FS_OpenMode#OPEN_CREAT; file_id : DINT; written_bytes : DINT; date_and_time : DATE_AND_TIME; year, month, day, hour, minute, second, millisecond : UINT; temp : STRING[5]; text : STRING; END_VAR; IF first_run = 1 THEN (* During the first run the MMC mode is set to a default value (external drive) *) first_run := 0; System.FileSystem.Async.SetMicroSdMode(0, MmcModeType#MMC_MODE_EXTERNAL_DRIVE); END_IF; ready := System.FileSystem.Async.GetMicroSdStatus(0); System.FileSystem.Async.GetMicroSdMode(0, current_mode); IF enable &lt;&gt; current_enable THEN (* When the &#39;enable&#39; global variable is modified the state of the MMC is set accordingly *) error := System.FileSystem.Async.EnableMicroSd(0, enable); IF error = System.FileSystem.ErrorCode.LIB_FS_OK THEN current_enable := enable; END_IF; END_IF; IF mode &lt;&gt; current_mode AND current_mode &lt;&gt; 0 THEN (* When the &#39;mode&#39; global variable is modified the mode of the MMC is set accordingly *) error := System.FileSystem.Async.SetMicroSdMode(0, mode); IF error = System.FileSystem.ErrorCode.LIB_FS_OK THEN current_mode := mode; IF mode = MmcModeType#MMC_MODE_EXTERNAL_DRIVE THEN partition := System.FileSystem.Enums.PartitionType#SdCard; ELSIF mode = MmcModeType#MMC_MODE_PUBLIC_PARTITION THEN partition := System.FileSystem.Enums.PartitionType#PublicPartition; END_IF; ELSE mode := current_mode; END_IF; END_IF; (* The following block of code is a simple state machine to manage the writing of a test file on the MMC. *) IF write_file = 1 THEN (* The name of the test file contains a progressive number from 1 to 99 and the current mode of the MMC. *) current_file_number := current_file_number + 1; IF current_file_number = 100 THEN current_file_number := 0; END_IF; IF mode = MmcModeType#MMC_MODE_EXTERNAL_DRIVE THEN filepath := System.Text.FORMAT(&#39;%02d-Ext_drive_test.txt&#39;, current_file_number); ELSIF mode = MmcModeType#MMC_MODE_PUBLIC_PARTITION THEN filepath := System.Text.FORMAT(&#39;%02d-Pub_part_test.txt&#39;, current_file_number); END_IF; (* The file is opened *) file_id := System.FileSystem.FileOpen(partition, filepath, openmode); IF file_id &gt;= 0 THEN write_file := 2; ELSE (* Error while opening the file *) write_file := 3; error := file_id; END_IF; ELSIF write_file = 2 THEN write_file := 3; (* The test file contains the current date and time. *) System.Timer.GetTime(date_and_time); SPLIT_DT(date_and_time, year, month, day, hour, minute, second, millisecond); text := System.Text.FORMAT(&#39;%02d-&#39;, day); temp := System.Text.FORMAT(&#39;%02d-&#39;, month); text := System.Text.CONCAT(text, temp); temp := System.Text.FORMAT(&#39;%d &#39;, year); text := System.Text.CONCAT(text, temp); temp := System.Text.FORMAT(&#39;%02d:&#39;, hour); text := System.Text.CONCAT(text, temp); temp := System.Text.FORMAT(&#39;%02d:&#39;, minute); text := System.Text.CONCAT(text, temp); temp := System.Text.FORMAT(&#39;%02d&#39;, second); text := System.Text.CONCAT(text, temp); written_bytes := System.FileSystem.FileWrite(file_id, text); IF written_bytes &lt; 0 THEN (* If something goes wrong the error is signaled *) error := written_bytes; ELSE error := 0; END_IF; ELSIF write_file = 3 THEN (* The file is closed *) System.FileSystem.FileClose(file_id); END_IF; (* Refresh UI *) SendVirtualKey(NO_KEY, 1); END_PROGRAM (* The following function triggers the writing of a test file on the MMC *) FUNCTION set_write_file IF write_file = 0 THEN write_file := 1; ELSE write_file := 0; END_IF; error := 0; END_FUNCTION GetMicroSdStatus(USINT) System.FileSystem.Async.GetMicroSdStatus &ndash; Check the status of the micro SD external drive. The &lsquo;unit&rsquo; input variable is the number of the peripheral. Its value is &lsquo;0&rsquo; if there is only one micro SD.
Returns &lsquo;1&rsquo; if the micro SD is inserted and ready to be accessed, &lsquo;0&rsquo; if it is not ready, &lsquo;2&rsquo; if the micro SD module is diabled and &lsquo;-1&rsquo; in case of error.
