allItems.description:
System.USB.UsbDeviceMode – Usb device mode

Members

Name
Description

CdcMode
Communication Device Class (CDC) mode: the USB port becomes a virtual serial port.

MtpMode
Media Transfer Protocol (MTP) mode: allows to transfer files to and from a Personal Computer.

NoneMode
USB device disabled

Examples

(* This example shows how to check the status of the connection with a USB device and
how to set and get its mode, by choosing one of the following options:
- CDC = Communication Device Class (virtual serial port)
- MTP = Media Transfer Protocol (file transfer with a personal computer)
- disabled
*)
USING System.UI;
USING System.USB;

VAR_GLOBAL
mode : System.USB.UsbDeviceMode := UsbDeviceMode#NoneMode;
device_ready : BOOL;
error : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR

PROGRAM Main
VAR
current_mode : System.USB.UsbDeviceMode := UsbDeviceMode#NoneMode;
result : BOOL;
first_run : BOOL := TRUE;
END_VAR;

IF first_run THEN
first_run := FALSE;
(* Read the configured mode from the device *)
System.USB.GetUsbDeviceMode(mode);
END_IF;

device_ready := System.USB.IsUsbDeviceReady();

(* The error, if present, must be manually removed from the UI *)
IF error = FALSE THEN
